 about\nhealth impacts and how ozone pollution forms in Colorado, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone-pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion during the afternoons and evenings both\nWednesday and Thursday.","ends":"2026-08-27T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Weld, CO; Adams, CO; Boulder, CO; Jefferson, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Larimer, CO; Broomfield, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ef315fc5f2168dfb17d9e2dcb4b1708f6edc711f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ef315fc5f2168dfb17d9e2dcb4b1708f6edc711f.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-27T17:52:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 271752 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 1152 AM MDT Thu Aug 27 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Thunderstorm coverage decreases Thursday and Friday with mainly isolated high-based showers/storms with gusty winds. - Temperatures return to the 90s Friday andSaturday across the plains. - Thunderstorm coverage increases for late Saturday and Sunday. && ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-27T09:36:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Today and tonight... Warmer and drier air will filter in today which will result in less coverage of showers and thunderstorms. Isolated storms should develop over the Front Range and I-25 Corridor this afternoon, however little if any rainfall is expected. Gusty erratic winds is possible with any high-based shower. LONG TERM DISCUSSION...Friday through Monday... We will stay warm th","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FW